load-readable-models-from-cache-snapshot

Lane: cross

Unit: synchronize-model-catalog-with-official-membership

ChildPatch: load-readable-models-from-cache-snapshot

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema-snapshot

Purpose: Serve personal-account model lists promptly from readable same-account snapshots and announce official online model membership changes in the TUI.

Requires: Unit:cross/materialize-model-catalog-from-local-file

Provides: Expose unfiltered cache snapshots for caller validation; prefer readable same-identity snapshots for Plus, Pro and ProLite ChatGPT model lists while retaining invalidation; observe successful applied online membership before local overlays; compare successive same-identity observations in the existing refresh worker and broadcast added and removed slugs; show one live TUI warning per nonempty delta without replay duplication.

Boundary: Native provider requirements, auth identity, refresh admission, discovery opt-outs, failure policy, cadence and worker lifetime remain intact; other account types retain fresh-cache behavior; local catalog overlays and instruction files remain with their owners; cache reads and local edits do not become online observations, and notifications do not enter exec output.

Verification: Cache and models-manager tests cover stale versions, identities, invalidation, scope and official-only observations; app-server model-list startup, refresh worker and broadcast tests cover prompt cached responses and deltas; TUI tests cover warning transcript and popup rendering, replay suppression and mode scope.

CrossGroup: model-catalog


